---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const updated = 'September 30, 2026';
const seoDescription = "TwitterTools terms of service: acceptable use of the free X (Twitter) tools, intellectual property policy and DMCA takedown procedure.";

---

<Base
  title="Terms of Service & DMCA | TwitterTools"
  description={seoDescription}
  path="/terms/"
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight sm:text-4xl">Terms of Service & DMCA</h1>
    <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-slate-500">Last updated: {updated}</p>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-8 text-slate-700">
      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">1. What TwitterTools is</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          TwitterTools is a collection of free, independent utilities for X (Twitter) content:
          downloaders, a thread reader, a character counter, a URL/ID parser and a search query
          builder. The service is provided "as is", without warranties of any kind.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          TwitterTools is <strong>not affiliated with, endorsed by, or sponsored by X Corp.</strong>
          "X", "Twitter" and related marks are trademarks of X Corp. and are used here only in a
          descriptive manner.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">2. Acceptable use</h2>
        <ul class="mt-2 list-disc space-y-2 pl-5">
          <li>Only use the tools on public posts that you have the right to view and save.</li>
          <li>Don't use the service to infringe copyright, violate privacy, or break applicable law.</li>
          <li>Don't attempt to overload, scrape or automate abuse of the site or its API (rate limits are enforced).</li>
          <li>Respect the rights of content authors: media is served directly from X's CDN and nothing is archived here.</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">3. No guarantee of availability</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          The downloader and thread reader rely on X's free, undocumented embed endpoint, which
          may change or stop working at any time without notice. We work around breakages when we
          can, but availability of data-dependent tools cannot be guaranteed.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">4. DMCA / takedown policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          TwitterTools does not host user content. Media files are streamed from X's own servers
          at the moment you request them, and post data comes from X's public embed endpoint.
          TwitterTools does not archive, index or redistribute content.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2">
          If you believe material accessible through this site infringes your copyright, send a
          notice to <span class="font-mono text-sm">dmca@twittertools.com</span> including:
          (a) identification of the copyrighted work, (b) the URL(s) of the post(s) involved,
          (c) your contact information, (d) a statement of good-faith belief, and (e) a statement,
          under penalty of perjury, that the information is accurate and you are the rights holder
          or authorized to act for them. Valid requests will be answered promptly; where the
          content lives on X's infrastructure, we additionally recommend filing a takedown with X Corp.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold">5. Changes</h2>
        <p class="mt-2">
          These terms may be updated as the toolkit grows; the "last updated" date above always
          reflects the current version. Questions: <span class="font-mono text-sm">hello@twittertools.com</span>.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
